    "question": "Josh had 100 gummy bear candies. He decided to give his 3 siblings 10 candies each. Then he gave half of the remaining candies to his best friend. If he only wants to eat 16 gummy bear candies, how many candies are left to be shared with others?",
    "gold": "19",
    "answer": "Josh gave a total of 3 x 10 = <<3*10=30>>30 candies to his siblings.\nHe was then left with 100 - 30 = <<100-30=70>>70 candies.\nHe gave 70/2 = <<70/2=35>>35 candies to his best friend.\nSo he had 70 - 35 = <<70-35=35>>35 candies left.\nSince he only wants to eat 16 candies, there are still 35 - 16 = <<35-16=19>>19 candies left to be shared with others.\n#### 19"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many gummy bear candies are left to be shared with others, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of candies given to Josh's siblings:**\n   Josh has 3 siblings, and he gives each sibling 10 candies.\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 10 = 30\n   \\]\n   So, Josh gives away 30 candies to his siblings.\n\n2. **Calculate the remaining candies after giving to his siblings:**\n   Josh originally had 100 candies.\n   \\[\n   100 - 30 = 70\n   \\]\n   So, after giving candies to his siblings, Josh has 70 candies left.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of candies given to his best friend:**\n   Josh gives half of the remaining candies to his best friend.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{70}{2} = 35\n   \\]\n   So, Josh gives away 35 candies to his best friend.\n\n4. **Calculate the remaining candies after giving to his best friend:**\n   After giving candies to his best friend, Josh has:\n   \\[\n   70 - 35 = 35\n   \\]\n   So, Josh has 35 candies left.\n\n5. **Calculate the number of candies Josh wants to eat:**\n   Josh wants to eat 16 candies.\n\n6. **Calculate the number of candies left to be shared with others:**\n   Subtract the number of candies Josh wants to eat from the remaining candies.\n   \\[\n   35 - 16 = 19\n   \\]\n   So, the number of candies left to be shared with others is 19.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]",
